      "id": "V41_R00_CONTACT",
      "status": "RESOLVED",
      "evidence": "The complete source plane and its wheel shadows moved 60 native pixels upward to [620,1050,960,523]. Both tyres meet clear stone in the actual native contact crop and final master/email page. There is no leaf overlap, disconnected gear or relocation of the landing into the playground."
    },
    {
      "id": "B1_DUST_VISIBILITY",
      "status": "RESOLVED_FOR_PART1_REVIEW",
      "evidence": "Four soft lavender-grey billows are visible in an ordinary reduced whole-page view, emerge from the threshold and spill over the front of the top red step. They have no eyes, face, star, pearl or symbolic spiral, and no rectangular backing or obvious halo. Independent exact audit-comparable measurement is 63 proof pixels / 0.291667 in and 2.2599406:1, exceeding 0.2 in / 2:1."
    },
    {
      "id": "BOUNDARY_METHOD_PRECISION",
      "status": "RESOLVED_WITH_EXPLICIT_LOCAL_REPAIR_SCOPE",
      "evidence": "The full uncropped world remains in place. Top 180 and bottom 300 source-world rows use a declared sine-squared boundary blend; not every panorama pixel is claimed exact. The central 9,633,792 geographic pixels are independently exact. Native and page-size seam inspections found no hard horizontal join, half cloud, detached/doubled pine silhouette or conspicuous double-exposed foreground contour. This bounded sky/foreground repair is distinct from a full-scene redraw."
    },
    {
      "id": "FINAL_FRESH_CLONE_BASELINE_DEPENDENCY",
