    "judgment": [
      "The revised arrival reads as a coherent establishing view of Sky Lagoon rather than a catalogue of objects. Water and route are now part of the story context.",
      "The original playground spacing, complete fixture supports and single attached swing seat remain clear. The castle's four towers, Roshan glass, doorway and bridge retain source identity at the authored shoreline anchor.",
      "The full world is smaller on the 7x5 page than in V40 because the geography is no longer cropped or compressed. Plane, playground and castle still read; their relationship is the purpose of this wider view.",
      "The brighter dust reads as a deliberate quiet clue rather than an almost invisible door line. Its visible billows, not isolated faint outlier pixels, carry the measured height.",
      "The email edition's arrival and dust retain legible vector captions and the relevant scene/clue details. No new visible displacement, alpha failure or disruptive compression defect was found in the inspected reading views."
    ],
